 Hello! I'm glad you asked for help with your PHP programming task. Based on your requirements, here's a custom function named `smart_sort_array` that you can use:

```php
function smart_sort_array($set, $order = 'ASC') { // Order can be either ASC or DESC
    $size = count($set);
    for ($i = 0; $i < $size - 1; $i++) {
        for ($j = 0; $j < $size - $i - 1; $j++) {
            if (($order == 'ASC' && $set[$j]['age'] > $set[$j+1]['age']) || ($order == 'DESC' && $set[$j]['age'] < $set[$j+1]['age'])) {
                $temp = $set[$j];
                $set[$j] = $set[$j+1];
                $set[$j+1] = $temp;
            }
        }
    }
    return $set;
}
```

This function takes two arguments: `$set`, which is the array that needs to be sorted, and `$order`, which is an optional argument that specifies the order of sorting. By default, the order is set to ascending (ASC). If you want to sort in descending order (DESC), simply pass 'DESC' as the second argument when calling the function.

The function uses a simple switching algorithm to sort the elements based on their age. The outer loop runs from the first element to the second last element, while the inner loop compares each element with its next element and switches them if they are not in the desired order.

